-- title:
--   The real Lie algebra generated by a set of Hamiltonians
-- statement:
--   For a set $S$ of operators on $\mathbb C^{\iota}$, let $\mathcal L(S)$ be the smallest **real** Lie algebra of complex $\iota\times\iota$ matrices, with bracket the commutator $[X,Y]=XY-YX$, that contains $iH$ for every $H\in S$:
--   $$
--   \mathcal L(S)=\operatorname{Lie}_{\mathbb R}\{\,iH : H\in S\,\}.
--   $$
--   For Hermitian $H$ the elements $iH$ generate the unitaries $e^{-iHt}$. This is the Lie algebra "generated" by a set of Hamiltonians in Lemma 7.3.2; §7.3.3 stresses that it is generated by Lie brackets and real linear combinations, not by products as in a complex associative algebra.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `LieSubalgebra.lieSpan ℝ (Matrix ι ι ℂ)` of $\{i\cdot H\}$, with the commutator bracket (`LieRing.ofAssociativeRing`).
-- source:
--   Bacon, Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1, §7.3.3, p.102 (PDF p.119); Lemma 7.3.2, p.103 (PDF p.120)

import Mathlib

attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

namespace BaconThesis.Commutant

/-- **The Lie algebra generated by a set of Hamiltonians.**
Bacon, *Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers*, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1,
§7.3.3, p.102 (PDF p.119), and Lemma 7.3.2, p.103 (PDF p.120): Hamiltonians generate a Lie algebra
"in the sense of a Lie algebra (Lie bracket, linear combination)", not in the sense of a complex
associative algebra "(multiplication, linear combination)".

For a set `S` of operators on `ℂ^ι`, `lieGen S` is the smallest **real** Lie subalgebra of the
`n × n` complex matrices (bracket `[X, Y] = XY − YX`) that contains `iH` for every `H ∈ S`; for
Hermitian `H` these are the generators of the unitaries `e^{−iHt}`.

**Formalization Note.** `LieSubalgebra.lieSpan ℝ (Matrix ι ι ℂ)` of the image of `S` under
`H ↦ i • H`; the real structure of `Matrix ι ι ℂ` comes from `ℝ → ℂ`, and the Lie bracket is the
matrix commutator (`LieRing.ofAssociativeRing`, a local instance in Mathlib; files using `lieGen`
enable it with the same `attribute [local instance 100]` line). -/
noncomputable def lieGen {ι : Type} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] (S : Set (Matrix ι ι ℂ)) :
    LieSubalgebra ℝ (Matrix ι ι ℂ) :=
  LieSubalgebra.lieSpan ℝ (Matrix ι ι ℂ) ((fun H => Complex.I • H) '' S)

end BaconThesis.Commutant


